  "question": {
    "text": "Which compound has antifluorite structure?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\r\n$\\mathrm{MnO}_4$\r\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\r\n$\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{O}$\r\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\r\n$\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{O}_2$\r\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\r\n$\\mathrm{Li}_2 \\mathrm{O}_2$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Anti-fluorite structure refers to an anion array with tetrahedral cations and the compound having $A_2 B$ formula have anti-fluorite structure. So, $\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{O}$ has an anti-fluorite structure in which $\\mathrm{Na}^{+}$ions occupy all the tetrahedral voids and $\\mathrm{O}^{2-}$occupy half of the cubic holes."
  }
}